Subject: Rebuilds the register property-read hit path around a 16-byte PIC entry and kind quickening

What this does
  Rebuilds the register property-read hit path around a 16-byte PIC entry and kind quickening.

Why we need it
  The register VM's inline property-read hit carried the whole cache entry - the prototype holder shape and the entry kind - through the hot path, and the kind had to be re-tested on every read to decide whether the cached slot belonged to the receiver or to a prototype.

What it adds
  `struct JSRegPIC` shrinks to the hot half (`shape`, `slot_off`, `kind`, `misses`) with the slot stored pre-scaled so the hit folds the `shl $4` away and the holder shape moved to a parallel cold `regvm_pic_holder` array on the bytecode; a filled OWN entry rewrites the opcode byte in place to `ROP_get_field_own`/`ROP_get_field2_own`, whose handlers have no kind load, no kind compare and no prototype branch, while the generic opcode remains the unfilled/miss form and the slow path rewrites the byte back.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
